% Broken rhythms on notes, rests and chords with a fermata.  The broken
% rhythm applies to the written lengths, and the fermata to the lengths
% that it gives.  brokenadjust() (store.c) compared the lengths with the
% fermata, so that Hc>d was "Cannot apply broken rhythm", and the bar check
% counted the length that the fermata had added before the broken rhythm,
% so that [Hce]>d e f was a bar too long.  Tune 2 plays them with
% %%MIDI fermatafixed, which adds one unit length, an eighth note.
X:1
T:Broken rhythms with fermatas
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
Q:1/4=120
K:C
Hc>d e f |c>Hd e f |c<Hd e f |Hc>>d e f |Hz>d e f |
[Hce]>d e f |d>[Hce] e f |[ce]>[Hdf] e f |Hc>Hd e f |]

X:2
T:Broken rhythms with fermatas, fermatafixed
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=120
K:C
%%MIDI fermatafixed
Hc2>d2 e2 f2 |c2>Hd2 e2 f2 |Hc2<d2 e2 f2 |[Hce]2>d2 e2 f2 |[c2He2]>d2 e2 f2 |]
